Back to BlogJanuary 27, 2026\n\n# DeepSeek OCR 2: Revolutionizing Document Intelligence\n\nImage: DeepSeek OCR 2 Visual Causal Flow\n\nDeepSeek has officially launched DeepSeek-OCR 2, a groundbreaking optical character recognition system that fundamentally shifts from traditional linear scanning to a model that interprets images with \"human visual logic\".\n\n## DeepEncoder V2: Visual Causal Flow\n\nAt the core of this release is the DeepEncoder V2 architecture. Unlike standard OCR tools that process documents strictly line-by-line, DeepSeek-OCR 2 employs a \"Visual Causal Flow\" mechanism. It dynamically rearranges image components based on semantic meaning, mimicking how a human reads a complex page—first understanding the global layout, columns, and relationships before diving into specific details.\n\nThis approach significantly improves performance on complex layouts, such as mixed text/structure documents and tables, by enabling the AI to &quot;see&quot; the global context first.\n\n## Unmatched Efficiency & Technical Specs\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDeepSeek-OCR - Browse Files at SourceForge.net (https://sourceforge.net/projects/deepseek-ocr.mirror/files/)\nciteturn31162search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; DeepSeek-OCR source code.zip  | 2026-01-27 (2026-01-27 03:45:14 UTC)  | 8.2 MB  | 3\n\nImage: DeepSeek-OCR\n\n# DeepSeek-OCR Files\n\n## Contexts Optical Compression\n\nThis is an exact mirror of the DeepSeek-OCR project, hosted at https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-OCR. SourceForge is not affiliated with DeepSeek-OCR.\n\nThe interactive file manager requires Javascript. Please enable it or use sftp or scp.\nYou may still browse the files here.\n\nDownload Latest Version DeepSeek-OCR source code.zip (8.2 MB) Add to Preferred Sources\n\nName  | Modified  | Size  | Info Downloads / Week\n--- | --- | --- | ---\nDeepSeek-OCR source code.tar.gz  | 2026-01-27 (2026-01-27 03:45:14 UTC)  | 8.1 MB  |